IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `crtpa-nouns`
IMPORT `crtpa-s5-s6-promisee`

-- Tests for sections 5 and 6.  Every expected value is written from the text of ss 5 and 6, with the reason
-- beside it, before the module was run.  In each call the inputs are, in order, those of the rule's GIVEN.

§ `Tests -- s 5`

-- "Section 2 does not affect any right of the promisee to enforce any term of the contract."
#ASSERT `s 5 section 2 affects a right of the promisee to enforce a term of the contract` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 5 section 2 affects a right of the promisee to enforce a term of the contract` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 6: the limbs and the duty`

#ASSERT `s 6(a) the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the third party's loss in respect of the term` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(a) the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the third party's loss in respect of the term` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(b) the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the expense to the promisee of making good to the third party the default of the promisor` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(b) the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the expense to the promisee of making good to the third party the default of the promisor` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- inputs: a term is enforceable by the third party under s 2; recovered (a) the third party's loss; recovered (b) the promisee's expense; proceedings brought in reliance on s 2 by the third party.
#ASSERT `s 6 the court or arbitral tribunal must reduce any award to the third party` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6 the court or arbitral tribunal must reduce any award to the third party` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6 the court or arbitral tribunal must reduce any award to the third party` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the promisee has recovered nothing of either kind: the where fails.
#ASSERT `s 6 the court or arbitral tribunal must reduce any award to the third party` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no term is enforceable by the third party under s 2: the where fails.
#ASSERT `s 6 the court or arbitral tribunal must reduce any award to the third party` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- proceedings not brought in reliance on s 2 by the third party: outside the duty.
#ASSERT `s 6 the court or arbitral tribunal must reduce any award to the third party` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6 the court or arbitral tribunal must reduce any award to the third party` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 6: the award after the reduction`

-- inputs: the four facts of the duty; the award before the reduction; the extent of the reduction the court thinks appropriate.
#ASSERT `s 6 the award to the third party after the reduction` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 1000 (JUST 300) EQUALS JUST 700
-- the ends of what a reduction can be: nothing, and the whole award.
#ASSERT `s 6 the award to the third party after the reduction` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 1000 (JUST 0) EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `s 6 the award to the third party after the reduction` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 1000 (JUST 1000) EQUALS JUST 0
-- beyond them, the text describes no reduction.
#ASSERT `s 6 the award to the third party after the reduction` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 1000 (JUST 1001) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6 the award to the third party after the reduction` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 1000 (JUST (0 MINUS 1)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the extent is the court's judgment and has not been stated.
#ASSERT `s 6 the award to the third party after the reduction` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 1000 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- the duty does not arise: no reduced award is stated.
#ASSERT `s 6 the award to the third party after the reduction` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 1000 (JUST 300) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6 the award to the third party after the reduction` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 1000 (JUST 300) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Assertions on the regulative rule where nothing stands (FULFILLED)`

-- A DEONTIC value can be compared in an #ASSERT on this binary only when it is FULFILLED (probed 2026-11-05).
-- the promisee has recovered nothing: the duty does not arise.
#ASSERT `s 6 the court or arbitral tribunal MUST reduce any award to the third party` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FULFILLED
-- the proceedings are not brought in reliance on section 2 by the third party: the duty is not in play.
#ASSERT `s 6 the court or arbitral tribunal MUST reduce any award to the third party` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED

§ `Traces -- the regulative rule (read by eye)`

-- the duty arises; the court reduces the award at time 3: the duty is discharged.
#TRACE `s 6 the court or arbitral tribunal MUST reduce any award to the third party` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court or arbitral tribunal` DOES `reduce the award to the third party` AT 3
-- the duty arises; nothing yet done: the duty stands.
#TRACE `s 6 the court or arbitral tribunal MUST reduce any award to the third party` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)
-- the duty does not arise (the promisee recovered nothing): fulfilled with nothing standing.
#TRACE `s 6 the court or arbitral tribunal MUST reduce any award to the third party` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)
